message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on costume accessory kits that are sets put up for retail sale. Festive articles fall under heading 9505, and costumes of textile materials are generally classified under 9505.90.6000. The classification of sets under GRI 3(b) depends on which component gives the set its essential character. For these kits the components are suspenders (6217 or 6212), bowties, a nose, a cap and eyeglass frames. Since the products are costume accessories for Halloween or dress-up, heading 9505 is most likely. Carnival or costume items such as these are classified in 9505.90.6000 ("Festive, carnival or other entertainment articles... other: other"). The ruling probably classified them there on the basis that they are costume accessories, and I am fairly confident in that.

The alternative is that each kit is classified by its essential character, such as the suspenders under 6217.10.9500. However, the "assortment of three different kits" were likely classified together under 9505.90.6000, and the tariff text for that subheading is "Other" (Festive, carnival or other entertainment articles, other).

{"hts_code": "9505.90.6000", "reason": "The costume accessory kits are festive/carnival entertainment articles of heading 9505, falling under the residual subheading for other such articles."}
